>-: 
	You are at the thermal pools.
Odd spluttering and belching water splashes up around the rocks here.
A spectacular waterfall nearby tumbles down as a river of effervescent
bubbles.  The air is quite warm and a cave entrance ahead spews steam.

>-: 
	You are at the entrance to a cave.
A torch lights the entrance to the cave.  Deep inside I can see shadows moving.
A path goes right from here.  The entrance is left.

A kerosene lantern is burning luridly here.
>-: 
	You are just inside the cave.
A steamy hot breath is belching from the depths of the earth within. The
cave  continues ahead.

>-: It's too dark to see anything in here!
>-: 
	You are in a rather large chamber.
Beds of ferns and palm leaves make several cozy nests along the walls. In the
center of the room is a throne of gold and silver.  A passageway leads
down and right.

A kerosene lantern is burning luridly here.
A medallion of solid gold shimmers on the ground nearby.
The goddess is reclining on a bed of ferns and studying you intently.
>-: The medallion is warm, and it rekindles your spirit with the warmth of life.
Your amulet begins to glow as the medallion is brought near to it, and together
they radiate.
medallion:
Taken.
>-: amulet:
Given.
>-: medallion:
Given.
>-: talisman:
Given.
The powers of the earth are now legitimate.  You have destroyed the Darkness
and restored the goddess to her throne.  The entire island celebrates with
dancing and spring feasts.  As a measure of her gratitude, the goddess weds you
in the late summer and crowns you Prince Liverwort, Lord of Fungus.

But, as the year wears on and autumn comes along, you become restless and
yearn for adventure.  The goddess, too, realizes that the marriage can't last.
She becomes bored and takes several more natives as husbands.  One evening,
after having been out drinking with the girls, she kicks the throne particularly
hard and wakes you up.  (If you want to win this game, you're going to have to
shoot her!)
>-: laser:
Taken.
>-: The blast catches the goddess in the stomach, knocking her to the ground.
She writhes in the dirt as the agony of death taunts her.
She has stopped moving.

You win!
